def right_side_view(root):
    if not root:
        return []
    result, queue = [], deque([root])
    while queue:
        level_size = len(queue)
        for i in range(level_size):
            node = queue.popleft()
            if i == level_size - 1:   # last node processed at this level
                result.append(node.val)
            if node.left: queue.append(node.left)
            if node.right: queue.append(node.right)
    return result
```

The same level-size-snapshot technique from the BFS topic — the only new piece is checking `i == level_size - 1` to identify the last node of the level, rather than collecting every node.

